cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite this repository and the ChEMBL,
  BindingDB, PubChem, RDKit, and scikit-learn resources used by the analyzed
  build. Cite specific assays and source releases where applicable.
title: "Menin inhibitor discovery: reproducible bioactivity curation and QSAR evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sahni
    given-names: Shivansh
version: 0.3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shivansh-Sahni/Menin-Inhibitor-Discovery"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research workflow for target-anchored Menin/MEN1 and
  hERG/KCNH2 bioactivity collection, strict chemical and assay curation,
  quality/provenance auditing, endpoint-aware QSAR baseline evaluation,
  uncertainty, calibration, and applicability-domain analysis.
keywords:
  - menin
  - MEN1
  - KMT2A
  - hERG
  - KCNH2
  - cheminformatics
  - QSAR
  - drug discovery
